// The benchmark's script runs to the end (E18b): `bench.kes` with every timed phase cut to one
// simulated second, in a quiet headless window. The fill and the edits' settling end on their
// own. Every phase line, the fill time, the edits line, the circle's marks and `done` appear.
// The headless clock is fake (each frame is 1/60 s, the work takes no time), so the timings
// here are zeros; the counts are real: 269 columns and 788 chunks fill the view, and the
// edits mesh 450 chunks (25 middle cells at 1 chunk and 25 corner cells at 8, each twice)
// besides the 24 the stream queued while the view settled. 369 of the 400 frames are used.
use { run_bench from bench }

main() {
    run_bench()
}
// env: KESTREL_HEADLESS=400
// env: KESTREL_HEADLESS_QUIET=1
// replace: bench.kes let FLY20_SECONDS = 20 => let FLY20_SECONDS = 1
// replace: bench.kes let FLY100_SECONDS = 20 => let FLY100_SECONDS = 1
// replace: bench.kes let CIRCLE_SECONDS = 300 => let CIRCLE_SECONDS = 1
// expect: phase fill frames 135 work_med 0 work_p99 0 work_max 0 wall_med 16.667 generated 269 meshed 788 gen_ms 0 mesh_ms 0 upload_ms 0
// expect: fill_ms 2233.334
// expect: phase fly20 frames 60 work_med 0 work_p99 0 work_max 0 wall_med 16.667 generated 19 meshed 68 gen_ms 0 mesh_ms 0 upload_ms 0
// expect: phase fly100 frames 60 work_med 0 work_p99 0 work_max 0 wall_med 16.667 generated 50 meshed 180 gen_ms 0 mesh_ms 0 upload_ms 0
// expect: phase edits frames 54 work_med 0 work_p99 0 work_max 0 wall_med 16.667 generated 7 meshed 474 gen_ms 0 mesh_ms 0 upload_ms 0
// expect: edits mid_ms 0 corner_ms 0
// expect: mark 0
// expect: mark 1
// expect: phase circle frames 60 work_med 0 work_p99 0 work_max 0 wall_med 16.667 generated 19 meshed 68 gen_ms 0 mesh_ms 0 upload_ms 0
// expect: done
